From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Meiser <peter.meiser@gmx.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:39:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] config.h: Enable SHA-384 and SHA-512

OpenSSH 8.3's configure checks EVP_sha256, EVP_sha384 and EVP_sha512,
but the prebuilt config.h only defines HAVE_EVP_SHA256. digest-openssl.c
then maps EVP_sha384 and EVP_sha512 to NULL, so every SHA-384/512 digest
fails. sshd cannot shield its host keys (SSHKEY_SHIELD_PREKEY_HASH is
SHA-512) and fails in accumulate_host_timing_secret: "Unable to shield
host key ...: unexpected internal error". The rsa-sha2-512 and
ecdsa-sha2-nistp384/521 algorithms, which config.h already enables, need
them too. BoringSSL provides both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I1920d665790c678fbc9e1ecab7e3aa6bf574d8e9
---
 prebuilt-intermediates/config.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/prebuilt-intermediates/config.h b/prebuilt-intermediates/config.h
index dd7adc6..9174f39 100644
--- a/prebuilt-intermediates/config.h
+++ b/prebuilt-intermediates/config.h
@@ -385,6 +385,12 @@
 /* Define to 1 if you have the `EVP_sha256' function. */
 #define HAVE_EVP_SHA256 1
 
+/* Define to 1 if you have the `EVP_sha384' function. */
+#define HAVE_EVP_SHA384 1
+
+/* Define to 1 if you have the `EVP_sha512' function. */
+#define HAVE_EVP_SHA512 1
+
 /* Define if you have ut_exit in utmp.h */
 #define HAVE_EXIT_IN_UTMP 1
 
